        "heading_intro": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Floating Deck Kits — Freestanding, No Attachment to the House",
            "class_heading": ""
          }
        },
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>A floating deck is freestanding: it rests on its own foundation rather than being ledger-attached to your home. That avoids cutting into the siding, and it keeps the structure independent of the building.</p><p>A-DIY floating deck kits ship with Tuff Block foundation blocks, so the deck sits on its own footings at 15 to 17 inches off the ground. The lumber is cut to length, the hardware is galvanized, and the whole thing assembles with a power drill in 8 to 16 hours.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
