    "ways": {
      "type": "multicolumn",
      "blocks": {
        "column_ways_1": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "image": "",
            "title": "Hire a deck contractor",
            "text": "<p>A contractor handles design, materials, permits, foundation, construction and cleanup. It is the right answer for a complex build, and it is the most expensive: you are paying a premium for time and labour, and timelines run to weeks.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": "",
            "enable_autoplay": false
          }
        },
        "column_ways_2": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "image": "",
            "title": "Build from raw materials",
            "text": "<p>Buying lumber, hardware and decking separately gives you the lowest upfront cost and the most work. You own the design, the measurements, every cut and the structural layout — typically across several weekends.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": "",
            "enable_autoplay": false
          }
        },
        "column_ways_3": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "image": "",
            "title": "Use an engineered deck kit",
            "text": "<p>A-DIY sits between the two. The structural design is already done and the components arrive prepared for assembly, so a standard build takes 8 to 16 hours and costs 30 to 50% less than hiring a contractor.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": "",
            "enable_autoplay": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "column_ways_1",
